# KNOWN GAP — 🚨 WHICH NAME THE VIEW IS SPELLED THROUGH DECIDES MEMORY SAFETY,
# and the CoW rescue ITSELF reads the freed buffer.
#
#     Vector[String] alias = v            # second name for the same collection
#     String s = alias.get(0).unwrap()    # view spelled through `alias`  -> rc 139 SIGSEGV
#     String s = v.get(0).unwrap()        # view spelled through `v`      -> rc 0, "hello"
#
# The two programs are otherwise IDENTICAL -- the `alias` bind is still
# present in the control, merely unused. Only the spelling of the receiver
# differs, and it decides whether the program segfaults.
#
#     C backend        : SIGSEGV, rc 139
#     C + --sanitize   : AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free in
#                        `gorget_string_copy_cow` <- main
#     LLVM backend     : SIGSEGV, rc 139
#
# ⚠⚠ THIS IS NOT A DETECTION FAILURE -- IT IS AN EMISSION-ORDER DEFECT
# (Core #15e Q5: "am I reasoning about emission, or emission ORDER?").
# The compiler DOES notice the conflict: `--clones=sites` reports
#     alias.gg:10:9  Vector[String]  CoW materialization
# at the mutation line. The rescue is emitted -- and then runs against an
# ALREADY-DANGLING pointer. So no amount of better analysis fixes this; the
# materialization has to happen BEFORE the invalidating push, not after.
#
# ⚠ THE REALLOC IS LOAD-BEARING: `v` must be pushed enough to force the
# backing store to reallocate (64x here) and the payload must be heap-FORCED
# via `mk`, never a literal. Fewer pushes or a literal payload is rc 0 on both
# spellings and proves nothing.
#
# SIBLING, same round, same "a name decides memory safety" shape but a
# DIFFERENT mechanism -- state the discriminator before merging them:
#   * `t0699` -- a user &self MUTATOR METHOD's NAME decides safety, because
#     the name is looked up in a hardcoded 26-entry MUTATING_METHODS list, so
#     the prescan never fires. That is a DETECTION failure.
#   * THIS -- the RECEIVER NAME of the VIEW decides safety, and detection
#     SUCCEEDS. The defect is WHEN the emitted rescue runs.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints `hello` regardless of which name the view
# is spelled through, on BOTH backends, ASan-clean.
# Measured 2026-08-27 by the R45 DEEP-1 scout; orchestrator-verified with the
# control run alongside and the clone report captured.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(mk("hel", "lo"))
    Vector[String] alias = v
    String s = alias.get(0).unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        v.push(mk("fill", "er"))
        i = i + 1
    print(s)
